WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.630
Rome, AD 64.

2
00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:07.880
A great fire burns through the city,
and rumour blames the emperor Nero.

3
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:13.240
Nero shifts the blame to a group the
crowds already hate: the Christians.

4
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:19.540
About 112, a Roman governor called Pliny
writes to the emperor Trajan with a problem.

5
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:22.310
He does not know whether
to punish the name itself,

6
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.490
or crimes attached to the name.

7
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.620
Rome tolerated many gods.

8
00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:31.530
So why did it put Christians to
death, and why only some of the time?

9
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:35.640
In this mission, you'll read Pliny's
letter and the emperor's reply.

10
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:38.600
Then you'll follow
persecution from Nero onwards,

11
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.040
and see how its nature changed.

12
00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.890
Your mission: find out why
Rome put Christians to death,

13
00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.760
and why only some of the time.
